WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.610
Three closed caskets on a table.

2
00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:03.400
Gold.

3
00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:04.390
Silver.

4
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:05.450
Lead.

5
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:10.720
The gold one reads: "Who chooseth
me shall gain what many men desire."

6
00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:14.180
Silver promises "as much as he deserves".

7
00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:15.360
And lead?

8
00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:18.020
Lead's words stay hidden for now.

9
00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:20.960
One by one, suitors step up to choose.

10
00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:22.760
The lids stay shut.

11
00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:25.740
So why should the plainest
box be the right one?

12
00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:29.990
In this mission, you'll see why a rich
heiress can't choose her own husband,

13
00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.100
because of her dead father's will.

14
00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:35.690
And you'll read the speech one
suitor makes before he chooses,

15
00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:37.260
line by line.

16
00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:41.510
Your mission: explain why the
dullest casket holds the prize.
